"comparison": "Both Intel and AMD disclose their accounting policies and material outcomes related to valuation allowances for deferred tax assets. Intel reported a massive $9.9 billion non-cash charge to income taxes for valuation allowances recorded on its net deferred tax assets in 2024, indicating a conclusion that recovery was not more-likely-than-not for those assets. AMD describes its policy for recording such valuation allowances when recovery is deemed unlikely, noting that if realization becomes more-likely-than-not, the allowance would be reversed resulting in a credit to income tax expense. While Intel’s disclosure highlights a specific, material negative charge event impacting consolidated results, AMD’s disclosure outlines the general judgment process for maintaining or reversing these allowances, confirming the same underlying tax asset recoverability assessment framework.",
